cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: >-
  METIMMOX-1: clinical effectiveness, cost-effectiveness and value of
  information of biomarker-guided immunotherapy in metastatic MSS/pMMR
  colorectal cancer
abstract: >-
  R code behind three secondary analyses of the randomised METIMMOX trial
  (NCT03388190): Cox models of biomarker-by-treatment interactions, a
  partitioned survival cost-effectiveness model of CRP- and TMB/BRAF-guided
  immunotherapy, and value-of-information analyses.
authors:
  - family-names: Geisler
    given-names: Benjamin P.
    affiliation: University of Oslo
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ben-geisler/METIMMOX-1"
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - colorectal cancer
  - immunotherapy
  - biomarkers
  - cost-effectiveness analysis
  - partitioned survival model
  - value of information
  - R
